<section class="sec" id="personas"><div class="wrap"><div class="intro rv"><h2 class="h2">Which one are you?</h2></div>
    <div class="cs rv"><div class="cs-switch" id="caseSwitch" role="tablist" aria-label="Which one are you?" style="--x:0"><span class="cs-ind"></span><button class="cs-opt" role="tab" id="cs-tab-0" aria-controls="cs-pane-0" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0"><span class="cs-t">I'm an Investor</span></button><button class="cs-opt" role="tab" id="cs-tab-1" aria-controls="cs-pane-1" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span class="cs-t">I'm a Creator</span></button></div>
    <div class="cs-pane on" role="tabpanel" id="cs-pane-0" aria-labelledby="cs-tab-0" tabindex="0"><div class="cs-grid"><article class="pcard"><div class="phead"><img src="/images/v2/av2.webp" alt="" style="object-position:50% 11%" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div class="pname"><h3>Marcus</h3><div class="pdesc">The Loyal Reader</div></div></div><p>Marcus pays for three investment newsletters and still can’t tell whose ideas actually work. When his favorite analyst moves to Delphi One, Marcus goes too. Now those ideas come with a Value, a counter-View and Olives, and the analyst’s model portfolio is one click away.</p><a class="ptry" href="https://app.delphi.one/?nav=login&amp;snav=register" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Try the app as</span> <span data-name="3">Marcus</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="pcard"><div class="phead"><img src="/images/v2/av3.webp" alt="" style="object-position:63% 32%" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div class="pname"><h3>Miles</h3><div class="pdesc">The Committee of One</div></div></div><p>Miles has run his own money for twenty years, and every call is his alone. What he misses is the room: analysts pitching ideas, someone arguing the other side. On Delphi One he picks his analysts, hears their pitches and makes the call.</p><a class="ptry" href="https://app.delphi.one/?nav=login&amp;snav=register" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Try the app as</span> <span data-name="6">Miles</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="pcard"><div class="phead"><img src="/images/v2/av4.webp" alt="" style="object-position:43% 32%" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div class="pname"><h3>Lucía</h3><div class="pdesc">The Crypto Skeptic</div></div></div><p>Lucía holds crypto and has followed enough confident voices on X to know talk is cheap. Here every analyst’s portfolio is built from real trades on-chain, and every idea comes with its counter-View. She reads the bear case before she buys.</p><a class="ptry" href="https://app.delphi.one/?nav=login&amp;snav=register" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Try the app as</span> <span data-name="4">Lucía</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></div></div><div class="cs-pane" hidden="" role="tabpanel" id="cs-pane-1" aria-labelledby="cs-tab-1" tabindex="0"><div class="cs-grid"><article class="pcard"><div class="phead"><img src="/images/v2/av1.webp" alt="" style="object-position:21% 32%" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div class="pname"><h3>Harry</h3><div class="pdesc">The Newsletter Veteran</div></div></div><p>Harry has written paid research for years and his subscribers renew. What he can’t show is why: there’s no record, only his word. Here his reasoning is judged on its merits, his past posts become Valuations with one click, and he prices his own memberships.</p><a class="ptry" href="https://app.delphi.one/?nav=login&amp;snav=register" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Try the app as</span> <span data-name="1">Harry</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="pcard"><div class="phead"><img src="/images/v2/av5.webp" alt="" style="object-position:55% 0" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div class="pname"><h3>Kai</h3><div class="pdesc">The Crypto Voice</div></div></div><p>Kai covers Solana on X, and people keep asking what he holds. X can’t give him a title: there’s no #1 on Solana there. Here there’s exactly one, it goes to reasoning, not volume, and his members can Replicate his model portfolio.</p><a class="ptry" href="https://app.delphi.one/?nav=login&amp;snav=register" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Try the app as</span> <span data-name="5">Kai</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="pcard"><div class="phead"><img src="/images/v2/av6.webp" alt="" style="object-position:85% 0" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div class="pname"><h3>Ana</h3><div class="pdesc">The Rising Analyst</div></div></div><p>Ana is sharper than most of the names with big followings, but nobody has heard of her. On X, reach wins. Here Olives judge her thinking, not her follower count, and the best analyst on an asset leads its page, whoever she is.</p><a class="ptry" href="https://app.delphi.one/?nav=login&amp;snav=register" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Try the app as</span> <span data-name="2">Ana</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></div></div></div><div class="center-btn case-go"><a class="btn-dark case-lab" href="https://app.delphi.one/?nav=login&amp;snav=register" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Pick your analysts</span></a><a class="btn-dark case-lab" href="/creators"><span>See how you get paid →</span></a></div></div></section>
